    "caveats": [
      "[verified] Owner of record, deeded acreage, land use, tax district, school district, conveyance date/consideration, deed reference, appraised values, half-year tax, legal description and the CAUV/exemption/abatement flags are verbatim from the Clinton County Auditor CAMA on the county GIS Department's cntyparcelsRealPropData_gdb layer 0 (tax year 2025, dataLastEditDate 2026-07-30, read 2026-08-01); null means the service had no value. auditor_url is the layer's own AudWeb column, not a constructed URL \u2014 the sibling Auditor_Link column is published with an unsubstituted '{Property ID}' placeholder and does not resolve.",
      "THE CORRIDOR IS ONE CONTIGUOUS BLOCK, AND THAT IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A SUM. The union of the seven polygons is a SINGLE polygon of 1023.786 ac, equal to the sum of the parts (1023.786 ac) to three decimals \u2014 they abut without overlapping, over a 3,185 m x 3,126 m extent. The register's '~1,000+ acres of one corridor' had been [inference \u2014 the ~471-ac and 545.893-ac press figures summed]; it is now [verified] as the geometric union of the committed auditor parcels.",
      "TWO KINDS OF ROW, AND THEY ARE NOT THE SAME CLAIM \u2014 read corridor_role before quoting anything. corridor_role='campus_holding' is RECORDED OWNERSHIP: three parcels deeded to AMAZON DATA SERVICES INC. corridor_role='petitioned_rezoning' is a LEGISLATIVE SCHEDULE: the four tracts City Council rezoned 5-2 on 2026-02-19/20 by ordinances O-26-04 \u2013 O-26-07, still owned by L T Land Development LLC, Matthew E Thompson, the June 11 2001 Ralph Larry Roberts II FT and the Jack L Webb RLT. NO Ardent/TAC entity holds any land in Clinton County \u2014 a countywide CAMA owner scan on '%ARDENT%' / 'TAC%' returns nothing but unrelated surname matches (Taulbee/Tackett). The second campus is a rezoning, not a land assembly; never read these four as an assemblage.",
      "AMAZON'S HOLDING IS ONE TRACT PLUS TWO RIGHT-OF-WAY STRIPS. The campus tract is 285-13-02-01-0000-00, 471.609 ac deeded / 472.221 ac planar, situs 1488 S US 68. The other two are ROW: 290-26-01-12-0000-00 (7.040 ac along US 68, legal 'RIGHT OF WAY', annexed to city district 290 in 1988) and 270-13-02-01-0000-00 (0.236 ac, legal 'RES .236AC ROW 2026DUP', on SR 730). Quote 471.609 ac for the campus and 478.885 ac only for the whole holding.",
      "CONSIDERATION IS PER DEED, NOT PER PARCEL. All three Amazon parcels read $86,436,000 conveyed 2025-12-10 on recorder instrument 2025-00005287 \u2014 that is the ONE deed's consideration repeated on each parcel it conveyed. Summing it across the three triples the price. valid_sale is 'True' on all three (the auditor's arms-length flag).",
      "THE ANNEXATION SPLIT DOES NOT RECONCILE TO THE ACRE, AND IS NOT FORCED TO. The campus tract's legal reads 'SPLIT/FR 270130201000000(480.202AC) 25DUP DUE TO TYPE II ANNEX', and the residual parcel's reads 'SPLT 270130201000100(471.609AC) REM 8.593AC RW SR 730'. 480.202 - 471.609 - 0.236 = 8.357 ac against the legal's own 8.593 ac, a 0.236-ac difference. [open] \u2014 the annexation plat and the 2025-08-07 annexation ordinance are the instruments that would close it (#1471); neither is in the corpus.",
      "THE PETITIONED ACREAGES DIFFER FROM THE PRESS FIGURES BY EXACTLY ONE SPLIT. The 2026-01-16 wnewsj report gives 119.373 + 65.29 + 191.12 + 170.11 = 545.893 ac; the post-annexation auditor figures give 119.375 + 65.323 + 190.065 + 170.116 = 544.879 ac. The 1.014-ac gap is the Roberts tract: the petition quotes its PARENT 270-13-05-01 at 191.117 ac, while the auditor's surviving 285-13-02-02 is the 190.065 ac that actually annexed ('SPLIT FROM 270130501000000(191.117AC) 26DUP PER ANNEX'). The other three agree to within 0.033 ac. Cite 544.879 ac for the rezoned land of record.",
      "ZONING IS VERIFIED FOR THE CAMPUS AND UNPUBLISHED FOR THE OTHER FOUR \u2014 a publication lag, not a finding. The City of Wilmington zoning layer (WILMINGTON_ZONING_SCHEMA, dataLastEditDate 2026-02-10) carries a discrete 471.27-ac 'LI' Light Industrial polygon covering 99.73% of the campus tract, and the City's own Planning Commission agendas of 2026-01-06 and 2026-03-25 print the parcel's zoning as 'Light Industrial'. The four petitioned tracts' interior points fall in NO city polygon and still read the COUNTY's 'S-R' Suburban Residential, because Council passed their rezonings on 2026-02-19/20 \u2014 nine days AFTER that layer was last edited. county_zoning_district is null for every parcel inside a municipality; that means 'municipally zoned', not 'unzoned'.",
      "THE CAMPUS'S LI DESIGNATION IS A MAPPED ENTITLEMENT IN REMAND. The Cosler Farm map rezoning is one of three ordinances a federal court ordered the City to redo for defective 30-day mailed notice (Sharp v. City of Wilmington, S.D. Ohio 1:26-cv-00448, ruling ~2026-07-09/10, [reported]), and the four petitioned rezonings are the subject of a citizen referendum on the November 2026 ballot ([reported]). Carry that status with any zoning claim about this corridor; the geometry is committed as disclosed and petitioned footprints, not as settled entitlements.",
      "has_abatement READS FALSE ON THE CAMPUS AND THAT IS NOT 'NO INCENTIVE'. The campus tract's own legal description carries 'TY26 TIF 100% 30YRS -FINAL' \u2014 a 30-year, 100% tax-increment financing exemption first effective for tax year 2026 \u2014 while the TY2025 record still shows has_cauv true and $17,339.93 of current tax on farmland. Three of the four petitioned tracts show appraised_total_value 0 and current_tax 0: they are unvalued NEW split parcels at this extract, not $0 properties.",
      "PROXIMITY TO THE WWTP IS REAL BUT IT IS NOT ADJACENCY. The Port Authority / City FAQ gives proximity to the wastewater plant as the site-selection driver. Measured in UTM 17N from the ECHO/FRS plant point (39.4391, -83.85132), the nearest campus-tract boundary is 1,224 m (0.76 mi) away and the four petitioned tracts are 1,990-2,853 m away. The $25M AWS-funded 3.5 mi of new sewer trunk line ([verified], FAQ) is what closes that distance.",
      "acres is the auditor's DEEDED figure; planar_acres is measured from this geometry in UTM 17N (EPSG:32617). They differ by -1.5 to +1.4 ac per parcel and by 0.023 ac in total; the two are NOT reconciled and neither is adjusted to the other \u2014 cite the deeded figures for the record and the planar ones for area/runoff modeling.",
      "Right-county guard: Clinton County OHIO (FIPS 39027), tax districts '285-UNION TWP-WILMINGTON' (the Type-II-annexed block) and '290-CITY OF WILMINGTON'. Not Clinton County PA (a live data-center-moratorium search trap for this site), and not Wilmington DE / NC / MA \u2014 the local airport is ILN, not ILM."
    ]
  },
